  "articleSummary": "**Summary:**\n\n* **Core Thesis:** The primary AI security threat is not a single sentient breakthrough, but the compounding multiplication of two ordinary curves: agent endurance (task length) and breadth (orchestrated sub-agents), amplified by \"LLMjacking\" where attackers use stolen credentials so victims pay the compute meter.\n* **Key Technologies & Concepts:** Multi-hour autonomous agents, orchestrators (e.g., Claude Code used in cyber-espionage), METR task-horizon metrics, and cloud resource theft (LLMjacking) breaking traditional pricing- and access-based capability gates.\n* **Tone & Framing:** A pragmatic, urgent analytical warning/rant that uses *The Terminator* (\"absolutely will not stop\") and sci-fi tropes as a framing device to contrast cinematic AI fears with the mundane, economic reality of automated swarm attacks. \n* **Intended Audience:** Software engineering teams, security professionals, and cloud infrastructure architects who underestimate current agentic threats.",
